{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 COLLECTION — WINNING-SPEC 4.7 "the way out"  ·  #env2-coll-goodnight  ·  section 7 of 7.

  4.7 in one line: the homepage's closing gesture, reused so the two pages rhyme — לילה טוב in Frank
  Ruhl Libre 900, OUTLINE ONLY, never filled, over collection.image at 80% opacity under a sky-4
  gradient at object-position 50% 70%; under it the cross-links as PLAIN ANCHORS ON ONE HAIRLINE —
  the other places by name, then לכל N המוצרים. On /all the four places instead. It sits directly
  above the Kalles footer, so it is the last thing on the page and it is a way out, not a wall.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- the three things it offers
  1. the other places  - one anchor per sibling collection, its own title and its own count.
  2. the whole catalogue - לכל N המוצרים, N = collections.all.products_count, never typed.
  3. the small step    - the licensed photo promise and the mailto call to action, rendered by
                         snippets/elmsnest-v2-pdp-photo-cta (the ONE file that holds both the
                         mailto and the wa.me branch, and that strips a channel claim from a label
                         a merchant types). This file never builds a URL and never writes a label.
  No newsletter, no social column, no policy list, nothing fixed to a corner: those belong to the
  Kalles footer directly below, and repeating them here is what makes a page feel like it ended twice.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- where the places come from
  Blocks of type place, max four, each a collection picker. The block whose collection IS the
  collection being viewed is skipped, so decor prints path/wall/spot and /all prints all four -
  one file, five URLs, no handle hard-coded anywhere.
  If no block carries a collection (a preset dropped in before the template is configured), the
  section falls back to the store's own collections list, skips the current one, skips "all", skips
  the empty ones, and takes at most four. auto_places turns that fallback off.
  Counts are the collections' own all_products_count. Nothing on this screen is typed: 6.19.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- the word
  The word is DECORATIVE and aria-hidden: it is the page's punctuation, not its content, and a
  screen reader that reads it would announce a farewell as a heading. Its stroke brightens with the
  lamp (.30 -> .62) and it is never filled - 3.2 and the homepage 4.8 both bar a filled display word
  at this size. Being outline-only it also cannot be measured for contrast as text, which is right:
  it carries no information.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- core REPORT 9.1
  .env2-section a{color:inherit} is (0,1,1) and outranks .env2-btn{color} (0,1,0), so an ANCHOR
  styled as the FILLED pill renders ink-on-glow at 1.21:1. There is no filled pill here: the links
  are plain anchors that set their own colour from this section's own selectors, and the photo call
  to action is the quiet .env2-link (or the outlined ghost) - never the filled one. Belt: the
  non-ghost .env2-btn anchor is given the ink colour explicitly, so it can not inherit its way into
  the bug even if a later hand adds one. Measured in _verify-goodnight.js: 0 failures.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- no JS / reduced motion
  Everything is server-rendered text and ordinary anchors. With JavaScript disabled the core leaves
  --lit at 1, so the garden is at its full 80% and the word is at its bright stroke immediately; every
  link is a real href and the call to action is a real mailto. JS does exactly one thing: hand the
  section root to the shared observer so the garden fades up over 2.4s when the page reaches it
  (3.3, "goodnight - the garden - on arrival"). Reduced motion: lit at once, no transition.

  Plumbing: elmsnest-v2-core (rendered by layout/theme.liquid on every template) supplies the tokens,
  the fonts, the .env2-* helpers, [data-lamp] and window.env2. The night ground is painted by
  elmsnest-v2-ground-collection, which elmsnest-v2-coll-scene renders once. This section renders no
  global, paints no background, reads no option axis and prints no price.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_here = ''
  if collection != blank and collection.handle != blank
    assign env2_here = collection.handle
  endif

  comment
    The places. Blocks first; the store's own list only as a fallback, and only when asked.
    A block whose collection is the one being viewed is skipped, which is what turns the four
    places on /all into the other three on a collection page, with no handle typed anywhere.
  endcomment
  assign env2_block_n = 0
  assign env2_seen = ''
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type != 'place'
      continue
    endif
    comment
      An unset collection picker is nil, and nil is compared through the string it RENDERS rather
      than as an object: a captured handle is empty for nil, for a deleted collection and for a
      picker nobody filled in, and it is never empty for a real one. That is one guard for all three.
    endcomment
    capture env2_bh
      echo block.settings.collection.handle
    endcapture
    assign env2_bh = env2_bh | strip
    if env2_bh == blank or env2_bh == env2_here
      continue
    endif
    assign env2_key = '~' | append: env2_bh | append: '~'
    unless env2_seen contains env2_key
      assign env2_seen = env2_seen | append: env2_key
      assign env2_block_n = env2_block_n | plus: 1
    endunless
  endfor

  comment
    The fallback list, built only when not one block carries a collection. It is printed from its own
    parallel arrays because there is no block behind it to hang shopify_attributes on; the block list
    above is printed straight off the blocks, so a block and its anchor can never drift apart.
  endcomment
  assign env2_place_titles = ''
  assign env2_place_urls = ''
  assign env2_place_counts = ''
  assign env2_fallback_n = 0
  if env2_block_n == 0 and section.settings.auto_places
    for env2_c in collections
      if env2_fallback_n >= 4
        break
      endif
      if env2_c.handle == blank or env2_c.handle == 'all' or env2_c.handle == env2_here
        continue
      endif
      if env2_c.all_products_count == 0
        continue
      endif
      assign env2_place_titles = env2_place_titles | append: env2_c.title | append: '~~F~~'
      assign env2_place_urls = env2_place_urls | append: env2_c.url | append: '~~F~~'
      assign env2_place_counts = env2_place_counts | append: env2_c.all_products_count | append: '~~F~~'
      assign env2_fallback_n = env2_fallback_n | plus: 1
    endfor
  endif
  assign env2_titles = env2_place_titles | split: '~~F~~'
  assign env2_urls = env2_place_urls | split: '~~F~~'
  assign env2_counts = env2_place_counts | split: '~~F~~'
  assign env2_place_n = env2_block_n | plus: env2_fallback_n

  comment
    The catalogue link. The number is collections.all.products_count and it is never typed: the
    merchant writes [count] and Liquid substitutes it, wrapped in bdi like every numeral on the page.
    On /all the visitor is already there, so the link is not printed.
  endcomment
  assign env2_all_n = ''
  if collections.all != blank and collections.all.products_count != blank
    assign env2_all_n = collections.all.products_count | plus: 0
  endif
  assign env2_all_url = section.settings.all_url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url
  assign env2_all_label = ''
  unless env2_here == 'all'
    if env2_all_n != '' and env2_all_n > 0 and env2_all_url != blank and section.settings.all_label != blank
      assign env2_all_num = '<bdi>' | append: env2_all_n | append: '</bdi>'
      assign env2_all_label = section.settings.all_label | escape | replace: '[count]', env2_all_num
    endif
  endunless

  comment
    The garden. The four collection.images are the only four in the family with no baked text and no
    cream ground, 3.6.4 - so the order is the merchant image, then this collection's own image, then
    the first place's image, which is what gives /all - a collection that owns no image - a
    photograph instead of a hole.
    Each candidate is judged by the URL it RENDERS, never by the object: a collection with no image
    yields nil on Shopify and an empty object elsewhere, and only the rendered url tells the two
    apart. BUT image_url on a nil image RAISES, and Shopify prints that error INTO the capture, so
    the capture alone would come back non-blank and the section would draw a broken img and never
    reach its own fallback (measured: every one of the five urls, an unset picker). The object test
    stops the filter from running at all and the scrub is the belt for any engine that still emits
    one. If the url is empty no img is printed and the section is the word on the night.
  endcomment
  assign env2_img = section.settings.image
  capture env2_src
    if env2_img != blank
      echo env2_img | image_url: width: 1800
    endif
  endcapture
  assign env2_src = env2_src | strip
  if env2_src contains 'Liquid error'
    assign env2_src = ''
  endif
  if env2_src == blank and collection != blank
    assign env2_img = collection.image
    capture env2_src
      if env2_img != blank
        echo env2_img | image_url: width: 1800
      endif
    endcapture
    assign env2_src = env2_src | strip
    if env2_src contains 'Liquid error'
      assign env2_src = ''
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if env2_src == blank -%}
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- if block.type != 'place' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign env2_img = block.settings.collection.image
      capture env2_src
        if env2_img != blank
          echo env2_img | image_url: width: 1800
        endif
      endcapture
      assign env2_src = env2_src | strip
      if env2_src contains 'Liquid error'
        assign env2_src = ''
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if env2_src != blank -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_pos = section.settings.image_position | default: '50% 70%'

  assign env2_mail_body = 'שלום, מצרף/ת תמונה של המקום שרוצים להאיר.'
  if collection != blank and collection.title != blank
    assign env2_mail_body = env2_mail_body | append: ' הקולקציה ששוקלים: ' | append: collection.title
  endif
  assign env2_cta_style = section.settings.cta_style | default: 'link'
-%}
<section id="env2-coll-goodnight" data-env2-coll-goodnight data-lamp class="env2-section env2-coll env2-coll-goodnight" dir="rtl" style="scroll-margin-top:90px;--env2-stars:.7" aria-label="{{ section.settings.big_word | default: 'לילה טוב' | escape }}">
  <div class="env2-stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {%- if env2_src != blank -%}
    <div class="env2-coll-goodnight__garden" aria-hidden="true" style="--env2-goodnight-pos:{{ env2_pos }}">
      <img class="env2-coll-goodnight__img"
           src="{{ env2_src }}"
           srcset="{{ env2_img | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ env2_img | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w, {{ env2_img | image_url: width: 1800 }} 1800w, {{ env2_img | image_url: width: 2400 }} 2400w"
           sizes="100vw" width="1800" height="1013" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="env2-wrap env2-coll-goodnight__wrap">

    {%- if section.settings.big_word != blank -%}
      <p class="env2-coll-goodnight__big" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.settings.big_word | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if env2_place_n > 0 or env2_all_label != '' -%}
      <nav class="env2-coll-goodnight__next" aria-label="{{ section.settings.links_label | default: 'להמשיך אל' | escape }}">
        {%- if section.settings.links_label != blank -%}
          <span class="env2-kicker env2-coll-goodnight__label">{{ section.settings.links_label | escape }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if env2_place_n > 0 -%}
          <ul class="env2-coll-goodnight__places">
            {%- comment -%}
              Printed straight off the blocks: the anchor and the block.shopify_attributes it belongs
              to are written in the same iteration, so a skipped block (the place you are standing in)
              can never shift a name onto the wrong theme-editor handle.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign env2_drawn = '' -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type != 'place' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign env2_bc = block.settings.collection -%}
              {%- capture env2_bh -%}{{ env2_bc.handle }}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- assign env2_bh = env2_bh | strip -%}
              {%- if env2_bh == blank or env2_bh == env2_here -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign env2_bkey = '~' | append: env2_bh | append: '~' -%}
              {%- if env2_drawn contains env2_bkey -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign env2_drawn = env2_drawn | append: env2_bkey -%}
              <li class="env2-coll-goodnight__place" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <a class="env2-coll-goodnight__a" href="{{ env2_bc.url | escape }}">
                  <span class="env2-coll-goodnight__name">{{ block.settings.label | default: env2_bc.title | escape }}</span>
                  {%- if section.settings.show_counts and env2_bc.all_products_count != blank -%}
                    <span class="env2-coll-goodnight__n"><bdi>{{ env2_bc.all_products_count }}</bdi></span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Bounded by the count the pre-pass produced, not by the array's length: Shopify's split
              drops a trailing empty field and other engines keep it, and an unbounded loop would
              print a fourth, empty, hrefless anchor wherever it does not.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for env2_t in env2_titles -%}
              {%- if forloop.index > env2_fallback_n or env2_t == blank -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
              <li class="env2-coll-goodnight__place">
                <a class="env2-coll-goodnight__a" href="{{ env2_urls[forloop.index0] | escape }}">
                  <span class="env2-coll-goodnight__name">{{ env2_t | escape }}</span>
                  {%- if section.settings.show_counts and env2_counts[forloop.index0] != blank -%}
                    <span class="env2-coll-goodnight__n"><bdi>{{ env2_counts[forloop.index0] }}</bdi></span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if env2_all_label != '' -%}
          <a class="env2-coll-goodnight__all" href="{{ env2_all_url | escape }}">{{ env2_all_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.step_line != blank or section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
      <div class="env2-coll-goodnight__step">
        {%- if section.settings.step_line != blank -%}
          <p class="env2-coll-goodnight__line">{{ section.settings.step_line | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
          <p class="env2-coll-goodnight__cta">
            {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-photo-cta',
                label: section.settings.cta_label,
                style: env2_cta_style,
                subject: section.settings.mail_subject,
                body: env2_mail_body,
                class: 'env2-coll-goodnight__photo' -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* ---------- 4.7 the way out: one outlined word over the garden, then two hairlines of plain anchors ----------
   The seventh and last shape on the page (do-not 20): scene photo+card · ruler numeral+rail ·
   bands five compositions · span rungs · ledger numbered rows · terms two columns · and this —
   a display word that is only an outline, with the way onward written under it in ordinary links.
   The section paints no background: the ground is the pixel-measured body gradient from
   elmsnest-v2-ground-collection, and the only things this file puts above it are the star layer at
   the 3.1 depth for this position (.70) and the photograph. */
.env2-coll-goodnight{padding-block:clamp(96px,11vw,150px) 44px;isolation:isolate;overflow:hidden;min-block-size:clamp(520px,60svh,760px);display:flex;align-items:flex-end}
.env2-coll-goodnight__wrap{position:relative;z-index:1;inline-size:min(var(--env2-w),100% - 2*var(--env2-gut))}

/* the garden: collection.image at 80% once lit, object-position 50% 70% (4.7), under a sky-4 veil.
   The veil is heaviest at the top seam — where the terms section above must not be cut by a hard
   edge — and at the foot, where the links are read; it thins across the middle band the word sits
   in, so the outline has a garden inside it rather than a flat night. The colour is #020306, which
   is --env2-sky-4; it is written as rgba here because a gradient stop needs the alpha and the token
   is a hex. */
.env2-coll-goodnight__garden{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:-1;pointer-events:none;opacity:calc(.8*var(--lit,1));transition:opacity 2.4s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1);-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(0,0,0,0) 0,#000 22%);mask-image:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(0,0,0,0) 0,#000 22%)}
.env2-coll-goodnight__garden::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(2,3,6,.92) 0,rgba(2,3,6,.46) 26%,rgba(2,3,6,.62) 58%,rgba(2,3,6,.9) 82%,rgba(2,3,6,.95) 100%)}
.env2-coll-goodnight__img{inline-size:100%;block-size:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:var(--env2-goodnight-pos,50% 70%);display:block;filter:saturate(1.06) contrast(1.04) brightness(1.08)}

/* the word: outline only, NEVER filled (4.7, 3.2). The 1.5px stroke brightens with the lamp
   (.30 -> .62) and a faint breath of glow sits behind it. It is aria-hidden — punctuation, not copy. */
.env2-coll-goodnight__big{margin:0 0 clamp(34px,5vw,68px);font-family:var(--env2-serif);font-weight:900;font-size:clamp(52px,10.5vw,164px);line-height:.86;letter-spacing:.01em;color:transparent;-webkit-text-stroke:1.5px rgba(244,238,227,calc(.3 + .32*var(--lit,1)));text-shadow:0 0 40px rgba(255,211,148,calc(.14*var(--lit,1)));transition:-webkit-text-stroke-color 2.4s .4s,text-shadow 2.4s .4s;white-space:nowrap;user-select:none}

/* hairline 1 — the places and the catalogue, plain anchors on ONE rule (4.7) */
.env2-coll-goodnight__next{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:6px clamp(24px,3vw,44px);padding-block-start:18px;border-block-start:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}
.env2-coll-goodnight__label{flex:none;align-self:center;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:500;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--env2-gold)}
.env2-coll-goodnight__places{flex:1 1 auto;min-inline-size:0;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:0 clamp(20px,2.6vw,38px)}
.env2-coll-goodnight__place{margin:0}
/* the 44px tap floor (6.13) is bought with padding on BOTH viewports; the rule under the word is a
   text-decoration so it tracks the glyphs whatever the padding does. */
.env2-coll-goodnight__a{display:inline-flex;align-items:baseline;gap:9px;padding-block:12px;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(16px,1.3vw,19px);line-height:1.4;color:var(--env2-ink);text-decoration:none;transition:color .3s}
/* the rule goes on the NAME, not on the anchor: a flex container does not pass its text-decoration
   down to its flex items, so an underline set here would draw nothing — and on mobile, where the row
   is justified space-between, it would have spanned the gap and read as a hairline, not a link. */
.env2-coll-goodnight__name{text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:6px;text-decoration-color:rgba(244,238,227,.3);transition:color .3s,text-decoration-color .3s}
.env2-coll-goodnight__a:hover,.env2-coll-goodnight__a:focus-visible{color:var(--env2-glow)}
.env2-coll-goodnight__a:hover .env2-coll-goodnight__name,.env2-coll-goodnight__a:focus-visible .env2-coll-goodnight__name{text-decoration-color:var(--env2-glow)}
/* ink-2, not mute: the count is read off a PHOTOGRAPH, and over a lit bulb in the path scene the
   mute grey measured 3.72:1 on a phone. Measured again at ink-2 in _verify-goodnight.js. */
.env2-coll-goodnight__n{font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:14px;color:var(--env2-ink-2);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.env2-coll-goodnight__n bdi{unicode-bidi:isolate}
/* inline-block, never inline-flex: the catalogue label is ONE run of text with a bdi inside it, and a
   flex container drops the whitespace between its items — לכל 27 המוצרים would set as לכל27המוצרים. */
/* a.… , not .… : the core's .env2-section a{text-decoration:none} is (0,1,1) and a bare class is
   (0,1,0), so a rule written the obvious way loses and the catalogue link renders with no underline
   at all — the same shape of defect as the ink-on-glow anchor in core REPORT 9.1. Measured. */
.env2-coll-goodnight a.env2-coll-goodnight__all{flex:none;margin-inline-start:auto;display:inline-block;padding-block:12px;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(15px,1.2vw,17px);line-height:1.4;color:var(--env2-ink);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:6px;text-decoration-color:rgba(244,238,227,.4);transition:color .3s,text-decoration-color .3s}
.env2-coll-goodnight a.env2-coll-goodnight__all:hover,.env2-coll-goodnight a.env2-coll-goodnight__all:focus-visible{color:var(--env2-glow);text-decoration-color:var(--env2-glow)}
.env2-coll-goodnight__all bdi{unicode-bidi:isolate;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}

/* hairline 2 — the small step: the licensed photo promise and the mailto. Quiet by design: it is a
   step, not the page's call to action, and the page has already made that offer once in 4.6. */
.env2-coll-goodnight__step{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:14px clamp(24px,3vw,44px);margin-block-start:4px;padding-block:20px 4px;border-block-start:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}
.env2-coll-goodnight__line{margin:0;flex:1 1 30ch;min-inline-size:0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(15px,1.25vw,17px);line-height:1.6;color:var(--env2-ink-2);max-inline-size:52ch;text-wrap:pretty}
.env2-coll-goodnight__cta{margin:0;flex:none;line-height:1}
/* core REPORT 9.1 belt: the ghost sets its own colour, and a filled pill ANCHOR — which nothing here
   renders — is given the ink explicitly so it can never inherit its way to 1.21:1. */
.env2-coll-goodnight .env2-btn--ghost,.env2-coll-goodnight .env2-btn--ghost:hover,.env2-coll-goodnight .env2-btn--ghost:focus-visible{color:var(--env2-ink)}
.env2-coll-goodnight a.env2-btn:not(.env2-btn--ghost){color:var(--env2-btn-ink)}
.env2-coll-goodnight .env2-btn{min-block-size:48px}
/* the photo link wears the section's own rule — a text-decoration that tracks the glyphs — instead of
   the core .env2-link border, which with a 12px tap pad would float as a second hairline under it. */
.env2-coll-goodnight .env2-link.env2-coll-goodnight__photo{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-block-size:44px;padding-block:13px;font-size:15px;color:var(--env2-ink);border-block-end:0;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:6px;text-decoration-color:rgba(244,238,227,.4)}
.env2-coll-goodnight .env2-link.env2-coll-goodnight__photo:hover,.env2-coll-goodnight .env2-link.env2-coll-goodnight__photo:focus-visible{color:var(--env2-glow);text-decoration-color:var(--env2-glow)}

/* ---------- mobile: the word first and smaller, then the two hairlines stacked, 44px+ everywhere ---------- */
@media (max-width:900px){
  .env2-coll-goodnight{padding-block:72px 32px;min-block-size:clamp(460px,72svh,620px)}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__garden::after{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(2,3,6,.88) 0,rgba(2,3,6,.46) 20%,rgba(2,3,6,.82) 44%,rgba(2,3,6,.93) 70%,rgba(2,3,6,.96) 100%)}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__big{margin-block-end:30px;font-size:clamp(46px,13vw,64px);line-height:.9}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__next{gap:2px 20px;padding-block-start:14px}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__label{flex:1 0 100%;align-self:auto;margin-block-end:6px}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__places{flex:1 0 100%;flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch;gap:0}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__a{inline-size:100%;justify-content:space-between;padding-block:14px;font-size:16px}
  .env2-coll-goodnight a.env2-coll-goodnight__all{flex:1 0 100%;margin-inline-start:0;padding-block:14px;font-size:16px}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__step{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:12px;padding-block:18px 4px}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__line{flex:1 0 100%;max-inline-size:none;font-size:15px}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__cta{flex:1 0 100%}
  .env2-coll-goodnight__cta .env2-btn{inline-size:100%}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
/* 4.7 the way out: the section root is the lamp — hand it to the shared observer so the garden
   fades from 0 to its 80% over 2.4s when the page reaches it (3.3, "goodnight — the garden — on
   arrival"). That is the whole of this section's JavaScript. Without window.env2, or with JS off
   entirely, --lit stays 1 and the garden and the word are at full strength from the first paint. */
(function () {
  function init(el) {
    if (el.__env2CollGoodnight) return;
    el.__env2CollGoodnight = true;
    if (window.env2 && window.env2.observe) {
      window.env2.observe(el);
    } else {
      if (el.hasAttribute('data-lamp')) el.classList.add('lit');
      el.querySelectorAll('[data-lamp]').forEach(function (l) { l.classList.add('lit'); });
    }
  }
  function boot(root) {
    (root && root.querySelectorAll ? root : document).querySelectorAll('[data-env2-coll-goodnight]').forEach(init);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () { boot(document); });
  else boot(document);
  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', function (e) { boot(e.target || document); });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

